-- title:
--   Idelic conjugates of orders in H[ℚ,a,b] are orders
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ satisfying [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11), that is: $1\in\Lambda$; $xy\in\Lambda$ whenever $x,y\in\Lambda$; the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $B$; and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $\beta$ be a unit of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ relative to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$, the additive subgroup of $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ a finite adele all of whose components lie in the corresponding adic completions of the integers. Then [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda\,\beta$, namely the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $B$ obtained by pulling back the additive subgroup $\beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ along $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$, again satisfies all four conditions of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   Classically this is the statement that $\Lambda^{\beta}=B\cap\beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ is an order of $B$, a member of the genus of $\Lambda$ (the left order of the locally principal right $\Lambda$-ideal $B\cap\beta\widehat{\Lambda}$); only the order property is asserted, not the further invariance statements. It is used throughout the quaternionic part of the development, for instance in the arguments that identify the orders attached to elements of Hecke sets as Eichler orders.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_conjByFiniteIdele.lean

